WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.658 --> 00:00:15.984
On Sunday a crowd waited outside the church before the service.

2
00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:19.505
Reverend Mordaunt stood at the door.

3
00:00:19.525 --> 00:00:25.208
"There are more people than usual today," he said to the village shopkeeper.

4
00:00:25.228 --> 00:00:31.572
"We've all heard a rumor that the earl is bringing Lord Fauntleroy to church," she said.

5
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.383
"Everybody wants to see the boy who'll one day own everything around here."

6
00:00:38.844 --> 00:00:41.725
Reverend Mordaunt gave the shopkeeper a polite smile.

7
00:00:41.745 --> 00:00:46.528
"The earl hardly ever comes to church," the minister thought.

8
00:00:46.548 --> 00:00:52.371
"He probably just wants to show off his grandson."

9
00:00:53.011 --> 00:00:56.794
The crowd parted to let a young woman walk up the path to the church.

10
00:00:58.334 --> 00:01:00.676
The shopkeeper studied the stranger carefully.

11
00:01:01.708 --> 00:01:04.069
"That must be Lord Fauntleroy's mother."

12
00:01:04.089 --> 00:01:08.812
"Yes, I believe it is," Reverend Mordaunt said.

13
00:01:09.933 --> 00:01:10.593
It took Mrs.

14
00:01:10.673 --> 00:01:13.935
Errol a few moments to realize that people were staring at her.

15
00:01:15.176 --> 00:01:18.097
As she walked to the church, she was thinking of Cedric.

16
00:01:19.838 --> 00:01:22.760
Yesterday he'd ridden his pony all the way to her cottage.

17
00:01:24.621 --> 00:01:25.982
She smiled at the memory.

18
00:01:27.202 --> 00:01:30.164
But her thoughts were interrupted by a woman in a red cloak.

19
00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:32.541
"Good morning, my lady!"

20
00:01:33.001 --> 00:01:34.602
the woman said, curtseying.

21
00:01:35.763 --> 00:01:38.145
Other women followed her example and curtsied.

22
00:01:39.826 --> 00:01:42.508
One man after another removed his hat as Mrs.

23
00:01:42.588 --> 00:01:43.409
Errol passed.

24
00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:47.032
Mrs. Errol felt puzzled.

25
00:01:48.172 --> 00:01:51.155
Then she blushed when she realized what was going on.

26
00:01:51.175 --> 00:01:55.017
"They're doing this because I'm Lord Fauntleroy's mother!"

27
00:01:55.478 --> 00:01:56.058
she thought.

28
00:01:56.078 --> 00:01:58.200
"Good morning!"

29
00:01:58.716 --> 00:02:01.157
she said shyly and bowed in return.

30
00:02:02.198 --> 00:02:05.879
Having always lived in America, she wasn't used to this type of attention.

31
00:02:05.899 --> 00:02:10.961
"It's embarrassing, but everyone means well," she thought.

32
00:02:10.981 --> 00:02:14.543
"I'm touched by how friendly the villagers are."

33
00:02:16.023 --> 00:02:20.205
Mrs. Errol had barely entered the church when the earl's carriage drove up the lane.

34
00:02:20.225 --> 00:02:22.606
"Here they come!"

35
00:02:23.667 --> 00:02:26.328
The news passed excitedly from one group to another.

36
00:02:29.152 --> 00:02:32.133
The carriage came to a stop, and a footman opened the door.

37
00:02:33.294 --> 00:02:36.095
A boy in a black velvet suit and hat jumped out.

38
00:02:37.416 --> 00:02:39.757
Every man, woman, and child stared at him.

39
00:02:41.217 --> 00:02:43.718
They didn't bother trying to hide their curiosity.

40
00:02:43.738 --> 00:02:47.140
"He looks just like the captain!"

41
00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.801
said a woman who remembered Cedric's father.

42
00:02:51.282 --> 00:02:56.204
As a footman helped the earl from the carriage, Cedric looked at his grandfather affectionately.

43
00:02:57.612 --> 00:03:00.553
"The earl of Dorincourt doesn't frighten that lad!"

44
00:03:01.914 --> 00:03:03.274
one man said with a chuckle.

45
00:03:03.294 --> 00:03:08.877
"Just lean on me," Cedric said to his grandfather.

46
00:03:08.897 --> 00:03:11.838
"Everyone is so happy to see you!"

47
00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:14.619
"Take off your cap!"

48
00:03:15.119 --> 00:03:18.521
the earl ordered his grandson as he leaned on the boy's shoulder.

49
00:03:18.541 --> 00:03:21.242
"They're bowing to you."

50
00:03:25.544 --> 00:03:26.204
"To me?"

51
00:03:27.392 --> 00:03:30.775
Cedric whipped off his hat and tried to bow to everyone at once.

52
00:03:30.795 --> 00:03:36.139
"They've heard how you helped that poor farmer," the earl said.

53
00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.282
The earl hadn't cared about the farmer.

54
00:03:40.383 --> 00:03:42.945
But it had amused him to let Cedric help the man.

55
00:03:44.186 --> 00:03:46.828
He also enjoyed that Cedric was popular with the tenants.

56
00:03:46.848 --> 00:03:50.451
"Good morning, Lord Fauntleroy!"

57
00:03:50.851 --> 00:03:52.452
cried the woman in the red cloak.

58
00:03:52.472 --> 00:03:54.834
"Long may you live!"

59
00:03:54.854 --> 00:03:56.936
"Thank you, ma'am!"

60
00:03:58.728 --> 00:04:00.889
Cedric led his grandfather into the church.

61
00:04:02.889 --> 00:04:06.910
When they sat down, Cedric was pleased to see his mother seated across the aisle.

62
00:04:08.951 --> 00:04:12.872
Cedric smiled at her, but the earl didn't even glance in her direction.

63
00:04:12.892 --> 00:04:17.534
"I hope Cedric will always be a good person," Mrs.

64
00:04:17.634 --> 00:04:20.334
Errol thought, watching her son and the earl.

65
00:04:20.354 --> 00:04:25.696
"Especially when he's the earl and has so much power over these people."

66
00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.242
After church Cedric walked home with his mother.

67
00:04:33.003 --> 00:04:37.106
As they sat down for lunch, Cedric noticed the fresh flowers on the table.

68
00:04:37.126 --> 00:04:43.830
"Flowers and fruit arrive every day from the castle," Cedric thought.

69
00:04:43.851 --> 00:04:47.493
"So Grandpapa must be fond of Mama.

70
00:04:48.674 --> 00:04:51.856
But I still don't understand why they've never met."

71
00:04:52.797 --> 00:04:54.758
Before he could ask anything, Mrs.

72
00:04:54.818 --> 00:04:57.060
Errol brought up the thoughts she'd had at church.

73
00:04:58.488 --> 00:05:02.111
"Cedric, I hope you'll always be brave, honest, and kind."

74
00:05:03.492 --> 00:05:04.933
She unfolded her napkin.

75
00:05:04.953 --> 00:05:09.276
"Then you won't hurt anyone, and you'll help many people.

76
00:05:10.457 --> 00:05:13.239
The world will be a better place because you were born."

77
00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:16.961
Cedric ran around the table to hug her.

78
00:05:16.981 --> 00:05:19.903
"I'll try, Mama," he said.

79
00:05:19.923 --> 00:05:24.627
"The world is a better place because Grandpapa's alive.

80
00:05:25.427 --> 00:05:26.328
That's for sure!

81
00:05:27.744 --> 00:05:30.867
When I grow up, I'll try to be just like him."

82
00:05:32.829 --> 00:05:37.593
After Cedric had returned to the castle, he told the earl about the conversation with his mother.

83
00:05:37.613 --> 00:05:43.338
"I said that you've made the world a better place, and that I want to be just like

84
00:05:43.398 --> 00:05:44.759
you," Cedric said.

85
00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:48.582
The earl shifted uneasily in his chair.

86
00:05:48.602 --> 00:05:52.525
"What did your mother say about that?"

87
00:05:54.007 --> 00:05:55.228
"She said that was right.

88
00:05:56.224 --> 00:06:00.691
And that we must always look for the good in people and imitate it."

89
00:06:02.053 --> 00:06:04.497
The earl was too surprised to reply.

90
00:06:05.759 --> 00:06:09.003
He had never expected such a kind response from Cedric's mother.
